Both English rows of a plural family were rewritten, and all FOUR
Russian rows are stale — not two.

`en.json` cannot legally carry "msg.done.few" or "msg.done.many": E15 holds each
language to exactly the CLDR categories it needs, and English needs one and
other. So a staleness reader keyed on `en.keys.get(key)` finds nothing for the
two Russian-only rows, skips them, and reports two of the four. The other two
ship describing English nobody writes any more, and `sync --accept` clears the
whole family in one gesture.

The two rows English cannot carry are anchored on "msg.done.other" instead —
the one category every language has. The digests here are real sha256 over the
English those Russian rows were made against, so this fixture also pins the
digest itself and not merely the comparison.
